  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Good labour practices benefit businesses by reducing turnover, enhancing productivity, and improving competitiveness. Following the 2021 military coup, numerous labour disputes emerged. The international community demands employers enhance human rights due diligence and improve labour and environmental standards (Recommendations of the Commission of Inquiry 2022-2023). 
The ILO continues to strengthen the capacity of employer organizations in enabling them to better serve their members, and to play a more impactful role in shaping socio-economic policies and complying with international labour standard in making sure businesses are aware of the risk of engaging child labour and trapping worker into forced labour condition. In this biennium, the ILO provides support on publication of Employer Guidebook on elimination of child labour as well as training roll out on the use of the guidebook.</narrative>
  </description>
